BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 679.0 Tm (ZFS was developed at Sun Microsystems in the early 2000s and introduced in Solaris during) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 662.0 Tm (2005, challenging the traditional division between filesystems, volume managers and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 645.0 Tm (independent RAID layers. It was subsequently published under open-source licensing and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 628.0 Tm (evolved into OpenZFS across multiple operating systems. Its design emphasised end-to-end) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 611.0 Tm (verification, large capacity and administrative simplification.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 582.0 Tm (The modern OpenZFS ecosystem supports pools and datasets rather than a single simple) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 565.0 Tm (filesystem volume. Snapshots, clones, compression, replication and multiple redundancy) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 548.0 Tm (arrangements emerged from an integrated transactional model. Exact feature flags and pool) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 531.0 Tm (format capabilities must be read from the installed implementation; historical Solaris and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 514.0 Tm (modern OpenZFS releases are not identical.) Tj ET
