BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 645.0 Tm (uberblock rings. An uberblock describes a committed root of a tree of object sets, block) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 628.0 Tm (pointers and data. Block pointers contain physical locations, sizes, birth transaction and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 611.0 Tm (checksums, so they verify a child from outside the child block itself.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 582.0 Tm (Copy-on-write means modified blocks are allocated anew and then reachable through newly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 565.0 Tm (published parent pointers. Transaction groups write the new tree and commit through a valid) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 548.0 Tm (uberblock. Dataset objects, metadata and indirect blocks form the logical namespace.) Tj ET
