BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 679.0 Tm (ZFS manages allocation at the storage pool level using metaslabs and space-map structures.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 662.0 Tm (Allocators select free regions from the pool and map writes through vdev geometry. Files) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 645.0 Tm (are described by DMU objects and block-pointer trees. Datasets provide separate properties,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 628.0 Tm (quotas and mount points; zvols expose block devices rather than ordinary directory trees.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 599.0 Tm (Snapshots reference past consistent trees; clones add a writable descendant, often sharing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 582.0 Tm (physical blocks. Compression and deduplication change physical space consumption.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 565.0 Tm (Copy-on-write metadata may increase write amplification for small random writes, but makes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 548.0 Tm (block sharing and replication practical.) Tj ET
