BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 679.0 Tm (ZFS verifies data and metadata using block-pointer checksums. When redundant good copies) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 662.0 Tm (exist, a read or scrub can replace corrupted blocks. A checksum can detect corruption) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 645.0 Tm (without being able to repair it if no valid replica survives. Synchronous writes use the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 628.0 Tm (ZFS Intent Log \(ZIL\), while normal asynchronous changes are grouped in txg commits. The ZIL) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 611.0 Tm (does not describe a universal redo log of all file data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 582.0 Tm (On import, ZFS chooses a valid committed uberblock and reconstructs the last consistent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 565.0 Tm (pool view. Pools have labels and redundant copies of critical metadata, but pool import,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 548.0 Tm (damaged-vdev recovery and resilvering are version- and topology-dependent. There is no) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 531.0 Tm (traditional fsck equivalent that rewrites all metadata for a classic non-COW image.) Tj ET
